==English==

===Alternative forms===
* (''Commonwealth spelling'') [[fervour]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|fervor|lang=la||a boiling or raging heat, heat, vehemence, passion}}, from {{term|fervere||to boil, be hot}}; see [[fervent]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-fervor.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{context|US}} An [[intense]], [[heated]] [[emotion]]; [[passion]], [[ardor]].
# {{context|US}} A [[passionate]] [[enthusiasm]] for some cause.
# {{context|US}} [[heat|Heat]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|passionate enthusiasm}} [[fire in the belly]], [[zeal]]

====Related terms====
* [[fervent]]
* [[fervid]]
* [[fever]]

